/**
 * THE v11 LOOT REVISION — every item the loot document carries, Act 1 through the last Act 4 drop.
 *
 * Transcribed from `Broken_Chain_Loot_and_Convergence_Focus_Actions_v11.docx`. v11 is the v9 full sweep
 * (Christopher, 2026-09-16: *"do a full sweep up to the act 4 items, this includes convergence output items"*)
 * with the Feywild Gifts revised — and he chose it: *"use version 11 and ensure that the 2 spell focus gifts are
 * correct in the app."* THE DOC IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH; this file is its transcription and nothing else belongs in it.
 *
 * WHY IT IS ITS OWN LAYER
 * -----------------------
 * The base library is an earlier publication and the app's authored export is a SNAPSHOT of what one
 * browser held. A revision written into the base alone could never reach the table: `mergeAuthored`
 * gives an authored copy the fields it states, and that export states nearly every one of these. So the
 * revision states its date, and the merge prefers whichever is NEWER — this file until the DM edits an
 * item in the app again, their copy from then on. See `equipmentLibrary.ts`.
 *
 * WHAT IS HERE: 124 rows — boss weapons and armour for both acts, the Act 2 quest path, merchant
 * stock and tavern consumables, the Ward Signet, 32 Convergence inputs (A1–A4), 6 Tier 1, 10 Tier 2,
 * 16 Tier 3 and 8 Tier 4 outputs, the Catalyst, and the 8 Feywild Gifts. Rimeguard is one adaptive armour
 * in the doc and three rows here, one per armour category, as it always was.
 *
 * THE GIFTS (v11). Each keeps the id it has always had, matched by its weapon form, so a Gift on a character
 * stays on it. Every WEAPON Gift is +2, adds PB and an extra 1d6 of its own type on each hit
 * (`chassisBonusDice`). Gift of First Light is a Quarterstaff and a +2/+2/+2 focus that adds 1d6 + PB to each
 * damage or healing roll of a Magic-action spell. Gift of Duskthorn is not a weapon at all: it is a CHARM bound
 * to a weapon the character carries (`bindsToItemId`, chosen on their bag), giving that weapon +2 and making it
 * a +2/+2/+2 focus, with a Thorn / Spell choice each turn. The rules live in `core/rules/giftFocus.ts`.
 *
 * ⚠ FIELDS ONLY THE DOC STATES. An entry carries its name, flavour, rules text, price, attunement, use
 * cadence and convergence labels; everything else — category, weapon dice, source encounter — stays the layer
 * underneath's, because the merge is field-wise. A Tier 3 row states its whole shape, because nothing
 * underneath has one.
 *
 * ⚠ AN EMPTY STRING AND A NULL ARE STATEMENTS. A pool that moved from "at dawn" to a rest states `note: ""`,
 * because a nested object merges key-wise and an unstated dawn note would survive. `null` REMOVES a field —
 * Duskthorn's old chassis, which the author export still states. See `mergeAuthored`.
 *
 * ⚠ FOCUS BONUSES FOLLOW ONE RULE: *"a spell focus at +2 would add +2 to the attack, +2 to the damage, +2 to
 * the spell dc"* (Christopher, 2026-09-16). The +1 focuses already carry +1 on all three.
 */
import type { EquipmentItem } from "../../core/ui/EquipmentBagEditor";

/**
 * ⚠ PARTIAL BY DESIGN. An entry states only what the document states about that item; the merge is
 * field-wise, so everything it leaves out stays as the layer underneath already had it. A `null` clears.
 */
export type LootRevisionEntry = { [K in keyof EquipmentItem]?: EquipmentItem[K] | null } & { id: string; name: string };

/** When this revision was published into the build (the v11 document's own date). Compared against the authored export's. */
